      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lincoln split from Smithfield in 1871 and was renamed to honor President Abraham Lincoln.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln%2C_Rhode_Island",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the late 1800s, Lincoln flourished as a mill town with textile factories lining the Blackstone River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lincoln%2C_Rhode_Island",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town has bought historic farmsteads and, in 1997, purchased Hearthside—a 1810 home—now being restored.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
